**Supervised Learning in Machine Learning**
Supervised Learning is a type of ML where the model is trained on labeled data — meaning every input has a corresponding correct output (answer).

Simple Analogy
Think of it like a student learning from a teacher:

Teacher gives questions with answers (labeled data)
Student studies the pattern
Student answers new questions on their own (prediction)
How It Works
Input Data (X)  →  [ML Model]  →  Predicted Output (Ŷ)
                        ↑
              Learns from Labeled
              Training Data (X, Y)


Steps:

Feed the model labeled training data (input + correct output)
Model learns the mapping function: Y = f(X)
Model is tested on new unseen data
Model predicts the output

